 "subject": "How to calculate Bruvo’s distance between groups",
 "messages_listed": 3,
 "last_activity": "2017-06-09T02:50:46Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "J6rmXC0bAQAJ",
   "from": "gang Ni",
   "author": "531e14cadec7ee46",
   "date": "2017-06-07T01:19:49Z",
   "subject": "How to calculate Bruvo’s distance between groups",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi everyone, <div><br></div><div>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">I am using poppr to analyses genetic patterns of a nematode species\r\nbased on microsatellites data.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:DengXian\">Two divergent groups appear\r\nin my study.  Now I want to calculate the Bruvo</span><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:DengXian\">’<span lang=\"EN-US\">s distances within each group and between two groups. I know </span></span><span style=\"font-family:DengXian;font-size:10.5pt;background-color:yellow\">bruvo.dist(popsub)</span><span style=\"font-family:DengXian;font-size:10.5pt;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"> can be used to generate </span><span style=\"font-family:DengXian;font-size:10.5pt\">intra-group result. But I have no idea about the </span><span style=\"font-family:DengXian;font-size:10.5pt\">script\r\nfor inter group distance.</span><span style=\"font-family:DengXian;font-size:10.5pt\">  Do you have any suggestions?</span><br></div><div><span style=\"font-family:DengXian;font-size:10.5pt\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:DengXian;font-size:10.5pt\">Many thanks.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:DengXian;font-size:10.5pt\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:DengXian;font-size:10.5pt\">Gang</span></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "peua_XzwAAAJ",
   "from": "Zhian Kamvar",
   "author": "d192ec4b1d416345",
   "date": "2017-06-08T14:28:45Z",
   "subject": "Re: How to calculate Bruvo’s distance between groups",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Gang,<div><br></div><div>Thank you for posting this to the forum. </div><div><br></div><div>If you want to find inter-group distance between two populations, you can convert the distance matrix into a square matrix and take the rows from population 1 and the columns for population 2.</div><div><br></div><div>An example:<br><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;poppr&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Aeut</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>bd </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> diss</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dist</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Aeut</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> percent </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># you can use bruvo&#39;s distance here</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>pop1_inds </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> pop</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Aeut</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">==</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Athena&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># getting a logical vector of indices for pop 1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>inter_distance </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pop1_inds</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">!</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pop1_inds</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># rows are group 1, columns are group 2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>boxplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">total </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> bd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">`inter-population distance`</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> inter_distance</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/zMAjheJ.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://i.imgur.com/zMAjheJ.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792480709834000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1htIF_yRFfcPgGRiXrW014\"><img src=\"https://ci3.googleusercontent.com/proxy/QE-sMRxjm1YlcZNiMDqAo_1eVO1VD_cjf1WLHD6XBv_QVR8k3pDG_3O_mhtEUqYtpg=s0-d-e1-ft#http://i.imgur.com/zMAjheJ.png\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"228\"></a></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\">Hope that&#39;s helpful.</p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\">-Zhian</p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><br></div><div><br></div><br>On Tuesday, June 6, 2017 at 8:19:49 PM UTC-5, gang Ni wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi everyone, <div><br></div><div>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">I am using poppr to analyses genetic patterns of a nematode species\r\nbased on microsatellites data.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:DengXian\">Two divergent groups appear\r\nin my study.  Now I want to calculate the Bruvo</span><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:DengXian\">’<span lang=\"EN-US\">s distances within each group and between two groups. I know </span></span><span style=\"font-family:DengXian;font-size:10.5pt;background-color:yellow\">bruvo.dist(popsub)</span><span style=\"font-family:DengXian;font-size:10.5pt;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"> can be used to generate </span><span style=\"font-family:DengXian;font-size:10.5pt\">intra-group result. But I have no idea about the </span><span style=\"font-family:DengXian;font-size:10.5pt\">script\r\nfor inter group distance.</span><span style=\"font-family:DengXian;font-size:10.5pt\">  Do you have any suggestions?</span><br></div><div><span style=\"font-family:DengXian;font-size:10.5pt\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:DengXian;font-size:10.5pt\">Many thanks.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:DengXian;font-size:10.5pt\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:DengXian;font-size:10.5pt\">Gang</span></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
